Object Get the tags Saved in <code>Actor</code> <code>actor-&gt;GetTags()</code> the world file, <code>"tags"</code> of the actor <code>Component</code> <code>component-&gt;GetTags()</code> the world file, <code>"tags"</code> of the component (a reserved key, like <code>"type"</code> and <code>"active"</code>) <code>World</code> <code>world-&gt;GetTags()</code> the world file, <code>"tags"</code> at its root <p>Each of them owns a <code>TagContainer</code>. Tags on a component let an actor say different things about its parts : the <code>PhysicsBody</code> of a door's handle tagged <code>Interaction.Door</code>, its frame not. Only these three carry tags : assets do not.</p> <pre><code>{
    "name": "Skeleton_03",
    "tags": ["Enemy.Undead.Skeleton", "Faction.Necromancer"],
    "components": [
        { "type": "physics_body", "tags": ["Hitbox.Head"], ... }
    ]
}
</code></pre> <p>Tags are not inherited down the actor hierarchy : the children of an actor tagged <code>Enemy</code> are not enemies. <code>Clone()</code> copies the tags of the actor and of its components.</p>
